Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:50:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/31] Metal: port ducc0's getNuNv cost model exactly (the
 w-layer root cause)

The cost model was missing the w-gridding terms ducc0 applies: fftcost *=
nplanes and gridcost *= supp when w-gridding, plus fftcost /= sigmoid(nthreads,
6, 2). Without them the kernel choice is a 2-D optimum, and ducc0's own verbose
output shows what that costs:

  ducc0: grid=(392x392x8) supp=7 dw=41.4668  (wmax-wmin)/dw=1.2057
  mine:  grid=352         supp=8 dw=46.4428  nplanes=9

nm1min matched (-0.0157) so the screen geometry was right; the kernel and grid
were not, making dw 12% wrong. That is the root cause of the w-layer failure -
the w-interpolation is quantised on dw, so a 12% error grows with w (0.8% field
rms at w=5, 3.7% at w=200, peaks decorrelated) - and it also explains the
residual 0.8% in the 2-D images, which was two different grids rather than two
different kernels.

diff --git a/metal/metalinversion.mm b/metal/metalinversion.mm
index 1e0d8519..bb3ce85e 100644
--- a/metal/metalinversion.mm
+++ b/metal/metalinversion.mm
@@ -33,36 +33,63 @@
